{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q416534","formula":"C₅H₁₂O₅","hill":"C5H12O5","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":5.0,"H":12.0,"O":5.0},"names":{"en":"Ribitol","ru":"Рибит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Ribitol, or adonitol, is a crystalline pentose alcohol (C5H12O5) formed by the reduction of ribose. It occurs naturally in the plant Adonis vernalis as well as in the cell walls of some Gram-positive bacteria, in the form of ribitol phosphate, in teichoic acids. It also forms part of the chemical structure of riboflavin and flavin mononucleotide (FMN), which is a nucleotide coenzyme used by many enzymes, the so-called flavoproteins.","ru":"Рибит (адонит, адонидодульцит) — C5H12О5 — пятиатомный спирт, остаток рибита, связанный с изоаллоксазином, входит в состав рибофлавина и флавинадениндинуклеотидов. Получен впервые Е. Мерком из адониса весеннего (Adonis vernalis) и исследован Е. Фишером. Входит в состав тейхоевых кислот клеточных стенкок грамположительных бактерий."},"fame":27,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"O[C@H](CO)[C@@H](O)[C@@H](O)CO","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":null,"atoms":22,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.909,"y":1.088,"z":-1.817,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.134,"y":-0.216,"z":-1.253,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.391,"y":-0.184,"z":-0.375,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.377,"y":0.952,"z":0.489,"el":"O"},{"x":0.155,"y":-0.695,"z":-0.545,"el":"C"},{"x":1.176,"y":-0.82,"z":-1.542,"el":"O"},{"x":0.615,"y":0.215,"z":0.621,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.237,"y":-0.023,"z":1.758,"el":"O"},{"x":2.087,"y":0.01,"z":1.018,"el":"C"},{"x":2.952,"y":0.705,"z":0.128,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.374,"y":1.717,"z":-1.225,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.318,"y":-0.888,"z":-2.1,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.513,"y":-1.099,"z":0.213,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.273,"y":-0.068,"z":-1